# Krezk's people at the Pool of the White Sun (lane 28, 2026-10-08: "more people walking around and doing things"):
# Widow Catrina lighting her candle at the water, and Old Simion keeping the graves. Unvoiced for now.

~ mourner
Widow Catrina: Every morning I tell him the news. The goats, the weather, who's fallen out with whom. The water never freezes, not even in the deep of winter. That's how I know he hears.
-> END

~ grave_keeper
if flag.sorin_fate == "pool"
Old Simion [sad]: The Krezkov boy, at peace in the water at last. I'll keep his stone straighter than all the rest. Don't tell the others.
-> END
endif
Old Simion: Stone suns, every one, so they face the morning. The snow pushes them crooked. I push them back. Between us we've kept it up for thirty years.
-> END
